title: What I did not do, and what surprised me
pid: 4ae64a17-4c15-44a4-9edd-75f2106f9541
body: |2-
  - The test of "owner of X" for a skgrepo that is not its owner's first
    is still nobody's: it needs a fixture whose dependencies manifest
    chains two foreign skgrepos, and this mission left no room.
  - Only the containers folder is redrawn. A replaced root keeps its
    other folders (subscribee, mentioners, aliases), the old node's
    members drawn noWarrant, and does not get the replacement's default
    subscribee folder. Same fault, same fix; Jeff did not ask.
  - Every reply in which the server writes a short message pays about
    40 ms of wall time on localhost, whatever the work: on a two-headline
    view a press took 41 ms of wall time for under 1 ms of CPU.
    'send_response_with_length_prefix' ('server/serve/util.rs') writes
    the header and the payload in two writes, and Nagle's algorithm holds
    the second until the client's delayed ACK. Not mine to change, and
    untested with the real clients; setting TCP_NODELAY on the socket,
    or writing header and payload in one write, would likely remove it.
    It belongs to whoever owns the server's TCP surface.
